WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.180
OK, it's Thursday, which means we do have
jobs numbers in the last week.

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.940
One point five million more people have lost
their jobs.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.640
Remember that this is once again a number
that before the Corona virus era would have

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:22.609
been twice the single week new unemployment
claim record, which was about 700000 prior

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:24.490
to coronavirus in one week.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:30.519
We have blown that out of the water for 13
straight weeks now.

00:00:30.519 --> 00:00:34.750
Record job losses peaking, of course, with
six point eight million people losing their

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.560
jobs in one week in late March.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.620
Then we saw declining to five million, four
million a week, three million, two million

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.370
in the last couple of weeks, about one and
a half million people each week lost their

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:48.370
jobs.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:54.320
So this brings the total number of jobs lost
during coronavirus to just over 45 million.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:01.129
Now, to put that number in context, before
the virus pandemic started, the workforce

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:04.030
was believed to be 158 million people.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:08.890
Forty five million jobs have been lost during
this pandemic in 13 weeks.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.070
And that is about 28 percent of the total
U.S. workforce.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:17.540
Now, it's very important to know and I have
no interest in hiding from you, obviously,

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:21.210
that some of the people who lost their jobs
have already found new jobs.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:26.620
So if you want to find good news or maybe
not terrible news.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.880
The job losses are decelerating, meaning each
week we have fewer people losing their jobs.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.180
That's good.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.009
Would be better to completely turn it around.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:43.649
We also, maybe most importantly, are seeing
that the last two weeks more people found

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:44.649
jobs.

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:49.229
In other words, they went back to work compared
to the number of people who lost their job.

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:53.799
So like even though in the last week, one
point five million more people lost jobs,

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:56.110
slightly more than that went back to work.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.329
So the total number of active unemployed people
actually went down.

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:01.190
It's a very small change.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:04.380
We went from twenty point six million unemployed.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.909
To twenty point five million unemployed.

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:12.310
OK, so that's important now to say it a different
way.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:16.630
Forty five million people total have lost
jobs during the pandemic.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:22.230
But 20 million are currently unemployed, meaning
a large number of people have gone back to

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:23.230
work.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.480
Now, what's the obvious problem?

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.980
The problem is we're in the middle of a pandemic.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.560
I know that Donald Trump is pretending as
though the pandemic is over.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.140
A lot of red states are pretending as though
the pandemic is over.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.230
We're going to hear in the voice mail segment
today from someone living in Hawaii.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.610
But we are still in the middle of a pandemic.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:46.090
The job losses are slowing down, which is
good, but the pandemic is raging and it's

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:49.410
actually worse than it has ever been in many
states.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:55.790
So here in the United States overall, we are
still finding about 20000 cases a day.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.990
The last few days, it's been more like twenty,
twenty three.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.400
Twenty four thousand cases.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:05.390
The seven day average of new cases is going
up, actually, and it has been going up for

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:06.390
10 days.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:12.560
But then you look at specific states, you
look at Texas, you look at Florida, you look

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:18.560
at Arizona and other states, they're spiking
dramatically and they appear to be nowhere

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.630
near their peak.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:22.470
So look at the contacts, right.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:30.020
If these job no jobs numbers that we are seeing
now are starting to be less bad because some

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.610
states are totally wide open.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.810
But corona virus is still raging.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:38.069
We have one of two possible futures.

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:42.799
Jobs continue to get less bad as way more
people die from corona virus.

00:03:42.799 --> 00:03:43.799
Right.

00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:49.879
We are to open the jobs improve, but deaths
absolutely get disastrously worse or we are

00:03:49.879 --> 00:03:51.330
going to have to shut down again.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.599
At least some states are going to have to
shut down again.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:56.030
And we are going to see the jobs numbers get
worse again.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:04:01.040
Now, we've seen some states like Texas, Texas
is seeing this.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.030
This is the worst week since the beginning
for Texas.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.209
Texas has made it pretty clear under their
Republican governorship that they don't have

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:11.489
an appetite to close down again.

00:04:11.489 --> 00:04:15.819
They seem to be taking the approach of it's
going to be what it's going to be.

00:04:15.819 --> 00:04:17.110
Protect yourselves.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:18.110
You don't want to go out.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.110
Don't go out.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.470
But we're opening and we're going to be staying
opening.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:26.850
What is becoming very clear is until you have
a really effective treatment and or a vaccine,

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:34.850
you can't have both a serious jobs recovery
and limit spread because some stuff needs

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:37.710
to remain closed, some stuff needs to remain
closed.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:43.430
I'm hopeful that here in Massachusetts, because
we've gone slowly, we have a very moderate

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:45.250
Republican governor here.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.050
He could have acted a little more quickly
early on, Charlie Baker.

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.090
But he widely has done a good job.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.090
We've gone.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:56.160
The planning has been phased and the phasing
has been planned, as I like to say, and we

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.540
have gone step by step and it's a slower recovery.

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:06.560
But the point is that hopefully it's a more
permanent recovery that will get us to have

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:12.190
some degree of economic record recovery up
to the point at which we have a vaccine and

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.320
or effective, effective treatment.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.500
Excuse me.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:21.160
And in some states, they are not taking precautions
and they're pretending everything's fine.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:26.720
And so while their jobs recovery may have
been faster in the immediate they're corona

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:31.270
virus cases and eventually deaths are going
to get really, really bad.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.870
And we would expect to see that probably by
the end of next week.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:40.570
You would see a lot of the cases from early
this week start tragically translating into

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:41.570
deaths.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.570
So we're going to follow it.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:42.571
OK

